    <item>
      <title>Pandas DataFrame Filtering: Techniques for Matching Lists and Patterns</title>
      <link>https://sqlpey.com/python/pandas-dataframe-filtering-techniques/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 04 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://sqlpey.com/python/pandas-dataframe-filtering-techniques/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;pandas-dataframe-filtering-techniques-for-matching-lists-and-patterns&#34;&gt;&amp;ldquo;Pandas DataFrame Filtering: Techniques for Matching Lists and Patterns&amp;rdquo;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;filtering-dataframes-based-on-exact-list-membership&#34;&gt;Filtering DataFrames Based on Exact List Membership&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;For scenarios where you possess a collection of exact identifiers (e.g., a list of &lt;code&gt;STK_ID&lt;/code&gt; values) that must be present in a DataFrame column, the &lt;code&gt;isin()&lt;/code&gt; method offers a straightforward and performant solution.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If your target list is &lt;code&gt;stk_list&lt;/code&gt;, filtering the &lt;code&gt;rpt&lt;/code&gt; DataFrame is achieved as follows:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-python&#34; data-lang=&#34;python&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;# Solution 1: Using the isin method for exact matches&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;filtered_rpt &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; rpt[rpt[&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;STK_ID&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;]&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;isin(stk_list)]&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;This approach generates a boolean Series indicating where each element in &lt;code&gt;&#39;STK_ID&#39;&lt;/code&gt; is present in &lt;code&gt;stk_list&lt;/code&gt;, which is then applied to filter the original data.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Pandas DataFrame Selection: Combining Multiple Boolean Conditions for Indexing</title>
      <link>https://sqlpey.com/python/pandas-boolean-indexing-multiple-conditions/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 04 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://sqlpey.com/python/pandas-boolean-indexing-multiple-conditions/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;pandas-dataframe-selection-combining-multiple-boolean-conditions-for-indexing&#34;&gt;&amp;ldquo;Pandas DataFrame Selection: Combining Multiple Boolean Conditions for Indexing&amp;rdquo;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This detailed exploration examines several accepted methods for applying complex boolean logic to select rows in a Pandas DataFrame.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;setup-for-demonstration&#34;&gt;Setup for Demonstration&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;First, let&amp;rsquo;s establish a sample DataFrame for testing these selection mechanisms.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-python&#34; data-lang=&#34;python&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; pandas &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; pd&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; numpy &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; np&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; random &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; randint&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;# Initialize a sample DataFrame&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;data_size &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;df &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; pd&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;DataFrame({&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;A&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;: [randint(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;9&lt;/span&gt;) &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; _ &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; range(data_size)],&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;B&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;: [randint(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;9&lt;/span&gt;) &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;10&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; _ &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; range(data_size)],&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;C&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;: [randint(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;9&lt;/span&gt;) &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;100&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; _ &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; range(data_size)]&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;})&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;print(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Initial DataFrame:&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;print(df